messages:
evan: heads-up i'm assembling a compact troubleshooting runbook that covers 429s, timeouts, and context-limit fallbacks. plan: one page, 3 tiny SDK cookbooks, and a small sim harness QA can run locally. draft PR: https://git.internal/redwood/docs/pulls/4999 :memo:

shay: love it. for the harness let's do a tiny Flask app with `/simulate?status=429&burst=5&delay=150` so QA can vary burst size and latency. include a docker-compose service. :whale:

mila: i'll write the UX blurb about fallback ordering: 1) backoff+retry (short-term), 2) trim context/prefix cache (preserve intent), 3) route to compatible cheaper model. one sentence tradeoffs each.

evans: can we include both `Retry-After` header parsing examples (seconds and HTTP-date)? many clients screw this up.

shay: node snippet i'll drop in PR comment:
```
// node pseudo
const res = await client.generate({prompt});
if (res.status === 429) {
  const ra = parseInt(res.headers['retry-after'] || '0', 10);
  await sleep((ra || backoff.next()) * 1000);
  return retry();
}
```

mila: short python fallback example (will add): check `response.headers.get('Retry-After')`, retry up to 3 times then call `trim_context()` helper. also note: prefer prefix-cache over blind trim.

qa-bot: lint: error-ref/compact-429.md line 21: missing fenced code language. line 45: use imperative present tense.

evans: noted. i'll fix style and add language markers.

shay: QA checklist suggestion: run `scripts/sim-429.sh --burst 10`, confirm header formats, assert metric `client.429.handled` increments, run stream-interrupt case. avoid time-based flakiness notes.

mila: assigning owners: evan (PR + prose + CI hook), shay (harness + node snippet), me (python snippets + UX blurb). i'll add a tiny curl example to the PR too.

evans: landing plan: PR open now, wait for snippets + CI harness, then tag `@eng-qa` for local smoke. aim to merge within 48h.

qa-bot: CI-smoke suggestion: add `docker-compose up --build` step to smoke job to exercise the harness.

evans: good call. will add. thanks all.
